rox 2.120$.\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\" data-cell-align=\"center\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$k \\setminus p$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$0.100$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$0.050$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$0.025$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$0.010$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$0.005$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$16$</td>\n<td>$\\,1.337\\,$ </td>\n<td>$\\,1.746\\,$ </td>\n<td data-fill=\"PapayaWhip\">$\\,\\color{blue}2.120\\,$ </td>\n<td>$\\,2.583\\,$ </td>\n<td>$\\,2.921\\,$ </td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$17$</td>\n<td>$\\,1.333\\,$ </td>\n<td>$\\,1.740\\,$ </td>\n<td>$\\,2.110\\,$ </td>\n<td>$\\,2.567\\,$ </td>\n<td>$\\,2.898\\,$ </td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$18$</td>\n<td>$\\,1.330\\,$ </td>\n<td>$\\,1.734\\,$ </td>\n<td>$\\,2.101\\,$ </td>\n<td>$\\,2.552\\,$ </td>\n<td>$\\,2.878\\,$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nSince we are considering both tails, our critical region is\n$T \\leq -2.120 \\qquad\\textrm{or}\\qquad T \\geq 2.120$.\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. Our test statistic ($1.649$) does not lie in the critical region, as shown below.![](images/07/07ba7bda0c0a235f900ebbfe1cdfdf11b717f27ad04e40fba71e4d17d6090f7c.png)\nSo, we do not reject the null hypothesis $H_0$. As a result, we conclude the following:$\\qquad$ *There is **insufficient** evidence that, at the $5\\%$ level of significance, we have $\\mu \\neq 5$.*\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139540366 17592186576411 true] [17592186171702 1074 "W