n=\"center\">$\\dfrac{1}{16}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n" 13194139540366 17592186576411 true] [17592186171875 1071 "Andrea has two dice. One of them is fair, and the other is not. The rolls of the unfair die follow the probability mass function $f(y)$ shown in the table below. What is the expected sum of the outcomes of $2$ throws of the fair die and $4$ throws of the unfair one?\n\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(y)$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{16}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{8}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{16}$ |" 13194139540366 17592186576411 false] [17592186171882 1074 "We can write down the binary integer using a place value chart:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"right\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"><strong>Place Values</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$2^3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$2^2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$2^1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$2^0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"right\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-bottom=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"><strong>Digits</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nTherefore, our number in base $10$ can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(1110)_{2} &= 1 \\cdot 2^{3} + 1 \\cdot 2^{2} + 1 \\cdot 2^{1} + 0 \\cdot 2^{0} \\\\\n&= 8 + 4 + 2 + 0 \\\\\n&= (14)_{10}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139540366 17592186576411 true] [17592186171882 1074 "We can write down the binary integer using a place value chart:\n\n| **Place Values** | $2^3$ | $2^2$ | $2^1$ | $2^0$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| **Digits** | $1$ | $1$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore, our number in base $10$ can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(1110)_{2} &= 1 \\cdot 2^{3} + 1 \\cdot 2^{2} + 1 \\cdot 2^{1} + 0 \\cdot 2^{0} \\\\\n&= 8 + 4 + 2 + 0 \\\\\n&= (14)_{10}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139540366 17592186576411 false] [17592186171883 1074 "We extract the powers of $2$ from the integer (starting from the largest possible one):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n53 &= 32 + 21 \\\\\n&= 32 + 16 + 5 \\\\\n&= 32 + 16 + 4 + 1 \\\\\n&= 1 \\cdot 2^{5} + 1 \\cdot 2^{4} + 0 \\cdot 2^{3} + 1 \\cdot 2^{2} + 0 \\cdot 2^{1} + 1 \\cdot 2^{0}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the corresponding place value chart is as follows:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"right\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"><strong>Place Values</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$2^5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$2^4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$2^3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$2^2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$2^1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$2^0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"right\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-bottom=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"><strong>Digits</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n(53)_{10} = (110\\,101)_2\n$$" 13194139540366 17592186576411 true] [17592186171883 1074 "We extract the powers of $2$ from the integer (starting from the largest possible one):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n53 &= 32 + 21 \\\\\n&= 32 + 16 + 5 \\\\\n&= 32 + 16 + 4 + 1 \\\\\n&= 1 \\cdot 2^{5} + 1 \\cdot 2^{4} + 0 \\cdot 2^{3} + 1 \\cdot 2^{2} + 0 \\cdot 2^{1} + 1 \\cdot 2^{0}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the corresponding place value chart is as follows:\n\n| **Place Values** | $2^5$ | $2^4$ | $2^3$ | $2^2$ | $2^1$ | $2^0$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| **Digits** | $1$ | $1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n(53)_{10} = (110\\,101)_2\n$$" 13194139540366 17592186576411 false] [17592186171884 1074 "First, we rewrite our decimal integer as follows:\n\n$$\n2^{3} + 2^{0} = 1 \\cdot 2^{3} + 0 \\cdot 2^{2} + 0 \\cdot 2^{1} + 1 \\cdot 2^{0}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding place value chart is given below:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"right\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"><strong>Place Values</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$2^3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$2^2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$2^1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$2^0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"right\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-bottom=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"><strong>Digits</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n(2^{3}+1)_{10} = (1\\,001)_2\n$$" 13194139540366 17592186576411 true] [17592186171884 1074 "First, we rewrite our decimal integer as follows:\n\n$$\n2^{3} + 2^{0} = 1 \\cdot 2^{3} + 0 \\cdot 2^{2} + 0 \\cdot 2^{1} + 1 \\cdot 2^{0}\n$